---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { createBreadcrumbSchema, createArticleSchema } from '../lib/seo';

const title = 'Solar Panels Cost UK (2024 Guide & Prices) | Solarpedia';
const description = 'How much do solar panels cost in the UK? Discover the average prices for 4kW to 10kW systems, installation costs, and expected savings.';
const keywords = 'solar panels cost UK, how much are solar panels, solar panel prices, cost of solar panels, 4kw solar system cost';
const path = '/solar-panels-cost';

const schema = [
  createArticleSchema({
    title,
    description,
    path,
    authorName: 'Solarpedia Research',
    publishedDate: new Date().toISOString(),
  }),
  createBreadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Solar Panels Cost', path: path },
  ]),
];
---

<BaseLayout 
  title={title}
  description={description}
  keywords={keywords}
  schema={schema}
  canonical={`https://solarpedia.co.uk${path}`}
>
  <div class="bg-brand-white pt-24 pb-20">
    <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4">
      <header class="text-center mb-16">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6">
          How Much Do Solar Panels Cost in the UK? (2024 Guide)
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-brand-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          A complete breakdown of average solar installation costs, battery prices, and what you can expect to pay for a typical UK home system.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="bg-brand-navy rounded-3xl p-8 text-center shadow-xl mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-white mb-4">Want to skip the averages?</h2>
        <p class="text-white/80 mb-6 max-w-xl mx-auto">
          Every roof is different. Use our independent calculator to see exact costs, system sizes, and payback periods tailored to your postcode and energy bill.
        </p>
        <a href="/solar-calculator" class="inline-block bg-brand-accent text-brand-navy px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-bold text-lg hover:bg-white transition-colors">
          Check My Solar Potential
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-lg text-brand-navy/80 max-w-none">
        <h2>Average UK Solar Panel Costs</h2>
        <p>
          In 2024, a typical residential solar panel system in the UK costs between <strong>£5,000 and £9,000</strong>, depending on the system size (kWp) and the quality of the components. 
        </p>
        <p>
          Here is a breakdown of estimated costs for standard roof-mounted systems (excluding battery storage):
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto my-8">
          <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b-2 border-brand-accent">
                <th class="py-4 px-4 font-bold text-brand-navy">System Size</th>
                <th class="py-4 px-4 font-bold text-brand-navy">Suitable For</th>
                <th class="py-4 px-4 font-bold text-brand-navy">Estimated Cost</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-4 px-4">3 kWp</td>
                <td class="py-4 px-4">1-2 Bed Home</td>
                <td class="py-4 px-4 font-bold">£4,500 - £5,500</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-4 px-4">4 kWp</td>
                <td class="py-4 px-4">3 Bed Home</td>
                <td class="py-4 px-4 font-bold">£5,500 - £6,500</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-4 px-4">5 kWp</td>
                <td class="py-4 px-4">4 Bed Home</td>
                <td class="py-4 px-4 font-bold">£6,500 - £7,500</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-4 px-4">6 kWp+</td>
                <td class="py-4 px-4">Large Property / EV Owners</td>
                <td class="py-4 px-4 font-bold">£7,500 - £9,500+</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2>What affects the cost of a solar installation?</h2>
        <p>While the averages above give a good baseline, your actual quote will depend on several factors:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Scaffolding:</strong> Included in most quotes, but complex roofs (e.g., conservatories underneath, multi-story) may require specialized scaffolding which increases costs.</li>
          <li><strong>Panel Quality & Efficiency:</strong> Premium panels (like SunPower or REC) cost more upfront but degrade slower and generate more power per square meter. Standard panels (like Jinko or Trina) offer an excellent middle ground.</li>
          <li><strong>Inverter Type:</strong> A standard string inverter is cheaper. Micro-inverters or DC optimizers (like Enphase or SolarEdge) are more expensive but essential if your roof suffers from shading.</li>
          <li><strong>Battery Storage:</strong> Adding a battery will increase your upfront cost significantly (usually by £2,500 to £5,000 depending on capacity).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Are solar panels VAT free?</h2>
        <p>
          Yes! The UK government introduced a 0% VAT rate on energy-saving materials, including solar panels and batteries (when installed together). This zero-rate policy runs until March 2027, making this an excellent time to invest in solar.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-brand-accent/20 p-6 rounded-2xl my-10 border border-brand-accent">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-0">Ready to get accurate pricing?</h3>
          <p class="mb-4">Don't rely on averages. Use our independent tool to calculate exactly what size system you need and how much it should cost.</p>
          <a href="/wizard" class="text-brand-navy font-bold hover:underline flex items-center gap-2">
            Calculate your costs now →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>